  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FCDO/OGB I Forest - India</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In January 2026, Fair Finance Asia (FFA) launched the Investing and Financing Outcomes in Regional Ecosystems and Sustainable Trade(I-FOREST) project&#x2014;a new regional initiative designed to contribute to the reduction of deforestation linked to Asian financing, trade, and consumption of forest-risk commodities. The project will run until March 2031.
Supported by the UK Foreign, Commonwealth &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; Development Office (FCDO) through its Forest Governance, Markets and Climate Programme Phase 2 (FGMC2), I-FOREST addresses a critical driver of forest loss: the overseas deforestation footprint of Asian economies as major importers, processors, and financiers of commodities sourced from tropical forest countries, including Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) member states.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="23">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CUTS Geneva, is a non-profit NGO that catalyses the pro-trade, pro-equity voices of the Global South in international trade and development debates in Geneva. Through its main three pillars, vis-&#xe0;-vis, international trade and development, regulations, and governance, CUTS has a robust history of working in areas such as regional integration, agriculture, environment, competition, investment and consumer protection, sustainability, gender, among others.
Since its establishment in 2008, CUTS Geneva has provided research-based advocacy and capacity building support through projects in the Global South - where it has real grassroot level networks and partners. CUTS today is well positioned as the prime interlocutor of developing countries and international organisations in Geneva.
In Geneva, CUTS collaborates closely with developing country trade experts and negotiators, backing them with technical knowledge and updates on the situation on the ground. CUTS is also the trusted technical cooperation and knowledge partner of international organizations such as the WTO and UNCTAD, where it has consultative status.
CUTS Geneva, along with its sister CUTS organizations in India,Kenya, Zambia, Vietnam, USA and Ghana have made footprints in the realm of economicgovernance across the developing world. Our activities stretch from Asia to Africa, South America and beyond.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CUTS International</narrative>
